    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nOn terminal clear, `[[` may jump to a \"ghost\" OSC 133 mark.\n\nThis issue can also be verified with `:marks nvim.terminal.prompt`\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n`nvim --clean`\n`:term`\n`seq 1 15`\n`clear`\n`seq 1 20`\n`[[` (with my prompt config this simply goes up a line, but in another shell this might be enough to trigger the issue)\n`[[`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`[[` does not jump to ghost marks.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1649+gc171a697cb\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nN/A\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch Linux 7.2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nfoot 1.28\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nAUR",
