            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> Is there a \"terminal clear\" event/sequence that the nvim.terminal.prompt docs example can listen to?\n\nI don't think so. In my setup, I get the following sequences when using `<C-l>`:\n\n```\n\u001b]133;A;click_events=1\n\u001b]133;B\n\u001b]0;~\n\u001b]133;A;click_events=1\n\u001b]133;B\n```\n\nAnd when issuing `clear`:\n\n```\n\u001b]133;C;cmdline_url=clear\n\u001b]0;clear ~\n\u001b]133;D;0\n\u001b]7;file://host/home/user\n\u001b]0;~\n\u001b]11;?\n\u001b]133;A;click_events=1\n\u001b]133;B\n```\n\nAs a workaround, I can make an autocmd to clear `nvim.terminal.prompt` when matching `\u001b]0;clear`, but it does not handle the `<C-l>`case. ",
            "created_at": "2026-09-22T01:52:35Z",
